### Phase 2 proof (R5.4) — run top to bottom against the local development database.
### Format: VS Code "REST Client" / Visual Studio / JetBrains HTTP client.
###
### Before running:
###   - @token      : a Backoffice JWT for the development environment.
###   - @airlineId  : the id of a selling airline that has NO Ancillary data yet
###                   (not the airline used for phase-1.http).
###   - @currencyId : the id of the currency to price in.
### The file registers its own sub codes, products and rules. Amounts are test data.

@host = http://localhost:4046
@token = PUT-A-BACKOFFICE-TOKEN-HERE
@airlineId = 11
@currencyId = 978

### 1. Enable 0CC (code only) — expect 200, "Active", "Industry"
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/ServiceSubCodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}}, "code": "0CC" }

### 2. Enable 0BX (code only) — expect 200, "Active", "Industry"
# @name loungeCode
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/ServiceSubCodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}}, "code": "0BX" }

### 3. Read 0BX — expect rfic "E", groupCode "LG", subGroupCode null, description1Code null,
###    description2Code null, commercialName "LOUNGE ACCESS"
GET {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/ServiceSubCodes/{{loungeCode.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Enable 0BX again, with an attribute — expect 422, code 16112 (the attribute rule is checked before the duplicate rule)
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/ServiceSubCodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}}, "code": "0BX", "rfic": "E" }

### 5. Enable the carrier-defined lounge code XLG — expect 200, "CarrierDefined"
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/ServiceSubCodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}}, "code": "XLG", "rfic": "E", "groupCode": "LG", "subGroupCode": null,
  "description1Code": null, "description2Code": null, "commercialName": "LOUNGE" }

### 6. Define the bag XBAG1 on 0CC — expect 200, "Draft"
# @name bag
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/AncillaryProducts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}},
  "productRef": "XBAG1",
  "type": "ExtraBaggage",
  "name": "First extra bag 23kg",
  "description": null,
  "salesScope": "TravellerBound",
  "quantity": { "unit": "Piece", "min": 1, "max": 1 },
  "document": { "type": "EmdAssociated", "rfisc": "0CC" },
  "codes": { "serviceTypeCode": "C" },
  "terms": { "refundable": false, "commissionable": null, "reusable": null, "formOfRefundCode": null, "interlineSettlementAllowed": null },
  "inventoryControl": "Unlimited",
  "baggage": { "pieces": 1, "weight": 23, "weightUnit": "Kg" },
  "lounge": null
}

### 7. Define the lounge LNGTHR on 0BX — expect 200, "Draft"
# @name lounge
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/AncillaryProducts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerAirlineId": {{airlineId}},
  "productRef": "LNGTHR",
  "type": "LoungeAccess",
  "name": "Lounge access",
  "description": null,
  "salesScope": "TravellerSegment",
  "quantity": { "unit": "Each", "min": 1, "max": 1 },
  "document": { "type": "EmdStandalone", "rfisc": "0BX" },
  "codes": { "serviceTypeCode": "F" },
  "terms": { "refundable": false, "commissionable": null, "reusable": null, "formOfRefundCode": null, "interlineSettlementAllowed": null },
  "inventoryControl": "Unlimited",
  "baggage": null,
  "lounge": { "airportIds": [1] }
}

### 8. Read the lounge — expect every field as sent, lounge.airportIds [1], baggage null,
###    document.rfic "E", codes.groupCode "LG"
GET {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/AncillaryProducts/{{lounge.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

